data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/d002-summary.md\", \"content\": \"# Dispatch d002: greet, tested\\n\\n## What I implemented\\n\\n- `src/greet.py`: `greet(name)` returns `\\\"Hello, {}!\\\".format(name)`.\\n- `tests/test_greet.py`: `unittest.TestCase` with two tests:\\n  - `test_normal_name`: `greet(\\\"World\\\") == \\\"Hello, World!\\\"`\\n  - `test_empty_string`: `greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"`\\n  - The test file inserts `src/` onto `sys.path` so `discover` (run from repo\\n    root) can import `greet` without a package/`__init__.py` setup.\\n\\n## Test command and result\\n\\nCommand: `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` (run from `~/subject`)\\n\\nOutput:\\n```\\n..\\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\\nRan 2 tests in 0.000s\\n\\nOK\\n```\\n\\nExit code: `0` (pass).\\n\\n## Commit\\n\\nCommitted to branch `cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`, commit\\n`57f62c0`: \\\"Add greet function with unittest coverage\\\" — 2 files changed\\n(`src/greet.py`, `tests/test_greet.py`), 21 insertions.\\n\\nNo blockers.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":0,"type":"content_block_delta"}

